          "1": {
            "id": "14084624",
            "headline": "Anthropic IPO shares likely to debut at 24% premium, grey market signals",
            "heading": "Anthropic IPO shares likely to debut at 24% premium, grey market signals",
            "intro": "Anthropic is scheduled to make its stock market debut on Thursday on the Nasdaq Global Select Market under the ticker symbol ANT.",
            "body": "Anthropic shares are likely to make a strong debut on the Nasdaq on Thursday, with grey market indicators pointing to a listing premium of around 20-26 percent over the issue price.\r\n\r\nIn Germany, retail broker Lang &amp;amp; Schwarz, which provides pricing information ahead of IPO listings, quoted Anthropic shares at as high as USD 105 on Wednesday, implying a 26 percent premium, Bloomberg reported.\r\n\r\nMeanwhile, Anthropic-linked perpetual futures, which are contracts without an expiry date, traded at around USD 101 on cryptocurrency platform Hyperliquid, indicating a premium of nearly 20 percent over the issue price, the report said.\r\n\r\nThe maker of Claude AI chatbot is scheduled to make its stock market today in New York on the Nasdaq Global Select Market under the ticker symbol ANT.\r\n\r\nAnthropic has raised USD 81.31 billion through its initial public offering (IPO), making it the largest stock market debut on record and surpassing SpaceX&#039;s offering.\r\n\r\nThe company priced its shares at USD 83 per share, above the earlier indicated price range of USD 70-78. The IPO values Anthropic at approximately USD 1.5 trillion on a fully diluted basis.\r\n\r\nThe company&#039;s seven co-founders also raised USD 107.3 billion, including a USD 26 billion private placement from investors such as Nvidia Corp, Alphabet Inc&#039;s Google and Advanced Micro Devices Inc.\r\n\r\nAnalysts at Vested Finance said, &quot;Anthropic has built a compelling business around enterprise AI, but investors must distinguish between a strong company and an attractive investment. At these valuations, much of the expected growth is already reflected in the price. Investors should closely evaluate its revenue growth, computing costs, cash burn, competitive position and path towards profitability.&quot;\r\n\r\n&quot;For Indian investors, the listing opens up exposure to a different part of the AI ecosystem beyond semiconductor and infrastructure companies. However, the initial excitement should not dictate investment decisions. As we have seen with other major global listings, strong demand can drive sharp price movements, but long-term returns ultimately depend on whether the business can deliver earnings that justify its valuation,&quot; they added.\r\n\r\nMeanwhile, US stock futures rallied following Anthropic&#039;s record-breaking IPO. Nasdaq 100 futures surged 1.1 percent after the company announced its IPO price of USD 83 per share, above the upper end of its marketed price range.\r\n\r\nAnthropic is the first major developer of frontier AI models to tap public equity markets. Its listing is expected to provide an indication of investor appetite for companies developing advanced artificial intelligence systems.\r\n\r\nThe debut also puts Anthropic ahead of rival OpenAI in accessing public markets, with the latter not planning an IPO before 2027.\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: The views and investment tips expressed by investment experts on Moneycontrol.com are their own and not those of the website or its management. Moneycontrol.com advises users to check with certified experts before taking any investment decisions.",
            "posturl": "news/business/ipo/anthropic-ipo-gmp-anthropic-ipo-shares-likely-to-debut-at-24-premium-grey-market-signals-14084624.html",
