            "intro": "Join us for Closing Bell on Moneycontrol as we wrap up the trading session on Thursday, November 19. The Nifty saw a U-turn after a cautious start and moved above 25,400, with a cooling-off in commodities lifting the market mood. Brent crude eased towards $93 a barrel, while gold and metals stayed under pressure after the sharp sell-off seen earlier in the day. Auto stocks revved up through the session and led the action among sectors. We break down the key sectors and stock-specific moves that shaped the day, the market breadth and how the broader indices fared, and the global cues from the Fed minutes, US bond yields and Asian markets. We also look at the FII and DII activity, what the Anthropic listing and the Trump-Xi-Putin meeting mean for sentiment, and what traders should watch for in the next session.",
